<section>
    <h2>Variables</h2>
    <p>unit.gl uses SCSS variables with the <code>!default</code> flag, allowing you to override them before importing
        the library.</p>

    <h3>Override Pattern</h3>
    <div class="code-block"><span class="comment">// _your-config.scss</span>
        <span class="comment">// Override variables BEFORE importing unit.gl</span>

        <span class="comment">// Custom base unit</span>
        $unit_base: 0.0625rem; <span class="comment">// Default: 0.0625rem (1px)</span>

        <span class="comment">// Custom typography scale</span>
        $scale_ratio: 1.25; <span class="comment">// Default: 1.618 (golden ratio)</span>

        <span class="comment">// Custom breakpoints</span>
        $breakpoint_md: 800px; <span class="comment">// Default: 768px</span>

        <span class="comment">// Then import unit.gl</span>
        @use "unit.gl" with (
        $unit_base: $unit_base,
        $scale_ratio: $scale_ratio
        );
    </div>

    <div class="alert alert--tip">
        <strong>Tip:</strong> Use the <code>@use ... with ()</code> syntax for the cleanest configuration pattern.
    </div>
</section>
